    ($SATQ$551c52b9$SATQ$, $SATQ$a1a5d2fd-4a30-4105-b4de-ee544853263c$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$725f71f7-77b3-4a2c-ac37-b3e0aea98c21$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Tilly earns <math alttext="p"><mi>p</mi>
</math> dollars for every <math alttext="w"><mi>w</mi>
</math> hours of work. Which expression represents the amount of money, in dollars, Tilly earns for <math alttext="39 w"><mrow>
	<mn>39</mn>
	<mi>w</mi>
</mrow>
</math> hours of work?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"6960bca9-8a0c-4a2c-bc9d-07aa4426f339","content":"<p><math alttext=\"39 p\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>39</mn>\n\t<mi>p</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"caa39cea-c2bf-4412-a704-dba6cb8f8f49","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction p Over 39 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mn>39</mn></mfrac></math></p>"},{"id":"4b92b729-52fb-4239-a6c9-8d030502030e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"p plus 39\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>p</mi>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>39</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"cad0ec10-1356-4d4d-8923-9cea84ab607d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"p minus 39\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>p</mi>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mn>39</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["6960bca9-8a0c-4a2c-bc9d-07aa4426f339"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that Tilly earns <math alttext="p"><mi>p</mi>
</math> dollars for every <math alttext="w"><mi>w</mi>
</math> hours of work. This can be represented by the proportion <math alttext="StartFraction p Over w EndFraction"><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi></mfrac></math>. The amount of money, <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>, Tilly earns for <math alttext="39 w"><mrow>
	<mn>39</mn>
	<mi>w</mi>
</mrow>
</math> hours of work can be found by setting up the proportion <math alttext="StartFraction p Over w EndFraction equals StartFraction x Over 39 w EndFraction"><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>39</mn><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>. This can be rewritten as <math alttext="39 p w equals x w"><mn>39</mn><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>w</mi></math>. Dividing both sides by <math alttext="w"><mi>w</mi>
</math> results in <math alttext="x equals 39 p"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mn>39</mn>
		<mi>p</mi>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>.&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This is the amount of money Tilly earns in dollars per hour, not the amount of money Tilly earns for <math alttext="39 w"><mrow>
	<mn>39</mn>
	<mi>w</mi>
</mrow>
</math> hours of work.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This is the amount of money Tilly earns for <math alttext="w"><mi>w</mi>
</math> hours of work plus <math alttext="39"><mn>39</mn>
</math>, not the amount of money Tilly earns for <math alttext="39 w"><mrow>
	<mn>39</mn>
	<mi>w</mi>
</mrow>
</math> hours of work.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This is the amount of money Tilly earns for <math alttext="w"><mi>w</mi>
</math> hours of work minus <math alttext="39"><mn>39</mn>
</math>, not the amount of money Tilly earns for <math alttext="39 w"><mrow>
	<mn>39</mn>
	<mi>w</mi>
</mrow>
</math> hours of work.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"551c52b9","external_id":"a1a5d2fd-4a30-4105-b4de-ee544853263c","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"725f71f7-77b3-4a2c-ac37-b3e0aea98c21","uId":"b46c091e-5dd7-4a5c-a2e6-0a9a2c2c7345","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.A.","skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Tilly earns <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> dollars for every <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math> hours of work. Which expression represents the amount of money, in dollars, Tilly earns for <math alttext=\"39 w\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>39</mn>\n\t<mi>w</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> hours of work?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"6960bca9-8a0c-4a2c-bc9d-07aa4426f339","content":"<p><math alttext=\"39 p\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>39</mn>\n\t<mi>p</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"caa39cea-c2bf-4412-a704-dba6cb8f8f49","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction p Over 39 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mn>39</mn></mfrac></math></p>"},{"id":"4b92b729-52fb-4239-a6c9-8d030502030e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"p plus 39\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>p</mi>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>39</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"cad0ec10-1356-4d4d-8923-9cea84ab607d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"p minus 39\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>p</mi>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mn>39</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["6960bca9-8a0c-4a2c-bc9d-07aa4426f339"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that Tilly earns <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> dollars for every <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math> hours of work. This can be represented by the proportion <math alttext=\"StartFraction p Over w EndFraction\"><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi></mfr