 alttext=\"39 w\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>39</mn>\n\t<mi>w</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> hours of work.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the amount of money Tilly earns for <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math> hours of work minus <math alttext=\"39\"><mn>39</mn>\n</math>, not the amount of money Tilly earns for <math alttext=\"39 w\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>39</mn>\n\t<mi>w</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> hours of work.</p>","origin":"manifold","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Tilly earns <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> dollars for every <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math> hours of work. Which expression represents the amount of money, in dollars, Tilly earns for <math alttext=\"39 w\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>39</mn>\n\t<mi>w</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> hours of work?</p>","externalid":"a1a5d2fd-4a30-4105-b4de-ee544853263c","templateid":"218a68c4-7103-4fa5-8152-640feef119ab","vaultid":"725f71f7-77b3-4a2c-ac37-b3e0aea98c21","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"6960bca9-8a0c-4a2c-bc9d-07aa4426f339","content":"<p><math alttext=\"39 p\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>39</mn>\n\t<mi>p</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"caa39cea-c2bf-4412-a704-dba6cb8f8f49","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction p Over 39 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mn>39</mn></mfrac></math></p>"},{"id":"4b92b729-52fb-4239-a6c9-8d030502030e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"p plus 39\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>p</mi>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>39</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"cad0ec10-1356-4d4d-8923-9cea84ab607d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"p minus 39\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>p</mi>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mn>39</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}],"correct_answer":["A"]},"createDate":1691007959830,"updateDate":1691007959830}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959830, 1691007959830),
    ($SATQ$555939d2$SATQ$, $SATQ$f9b50fe8-25d0-4faa-ad54-7ba7d01af7db$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">A cable provider wanted to know how many of its <math alttext="30,000"><mn>30,000</mn>
</math> customers would be interested in a new service plan. The provider selected <math alttext="300"><mn>300</mn>
</math> customers at random and asked each customer whether the customer would be interested in the new plan. Of those surveyed, <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math> said they would be interested. Which of the following is the best estimate of the total number of customers who would be interested in the new service plan?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"61453ae7-dd4c-432e-9683-21b67bac9eda","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"dfcce82e-e72e-4aa7-b1c3-3e01417b5e32","content":"<p><math alttext=\"80\"><mn>80</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"90bb05cc-6fad-4d2b-a330-091b0d54016d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"800\"><mn>800</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3ec26af9-2692-40b2-a60b-2a5ddafbe528","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8,000\"><mn>8,000</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["90bb05cc-6fad-4d2b-a330-091b0d54016d"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. It&rsquo;s given that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="8"><mn>8</mn></math> out of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="300"><mn>300</mn></math> customers in a random sample said they would be interested in the new plan. This means the fraction of sampled customers who said they would be interested is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction 8 Over 300 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>300</mn></mfrac></math>. Multiplying this fraction by the total customer population yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis StartFraction 8 Over 300 EndFraction right parenthesis left parenthesis 30,000 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>300</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>30,000</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="800"><mn>800</mn></math>. Therefore, the best estimate of the total number of customers who would be interested in the new service plan is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="800"><mn>800</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is the number of customers surveyed who said they would be interested in the new plan, not the best estimate of the total number of customers who would be interested in the new plan.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"555939d2","external_id":"f9b50fe8-25d0-4faa-ad54-7ba7d01af7db","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"066c631f-e26b-4e64-af24-c4c18de42476","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.A.","skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A cable provider wanted to know how many of its <math alttext=\"30,000\"><mn>30,000</mn>\n</math> customers would be interested in a new service plan. The provider selected <math alttext=\"300\"><mn>300</mn>\n</math> customers at random and asked each customer whether the customer would be interested in the new plan. Of those surveyed, <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math> said they would be interested. Which of the following is the best estimate of the total number of customers who would be interested in the new service plan?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"61453ae7-dd4c-432e-9683-21b67bac9eda","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"dfcce82e-e72e-4aa7-b1c3-3e01417b5e32","content":"<p><math alttext=\"80\"><mn>80</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"90bb05cc-6fad-4d2b-a330-091b0d54016d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"800\"><mn>800</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3ec26af9-2692-40b2-a60b-2a5ddafbe528","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8,000\"><mn>8,000</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["90bb05cc-6fad-4d2b-a330-091b0d54016d"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. It&rsquo;s given that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math> out of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"300\"><mn>300</mn></ma