":"E"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A cable provider wanted to know how many of its <math alttext=\"30,000\"><mn>30,000</mn>\n</math> customers would be interested in a new service plan. The provider selected <math alttext=\"300\"><mn>300</mn>\n</math> customers at random and asked each customer whether the customer would be interested in the new plan. Of those surveyed, <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math> said they would be interested. Which of the following is the best estimate of the total number of customers who would be interested in the new service plan?</p>","keys":["90bb05cc-6fad-4d2b-a330-091b0d54016d"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"61453ae7-dd4c-432e-9683-21b67bac9eda","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"dfcce82e-e72e-4aa7-b1c3-3e01417b5e32","content":"<p><math alttext=\"80\"><mn>80</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"90bb05cc-6fad-4d2b-a330-091b0d54016d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"800\"><mn>800</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3ec26af9-2692-40b2-a60b-2a5ddafbe528","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8,000\"><mn>8,000</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. It&rsquo;s given that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math> out of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"300\"><mn>300</mn></math> customers in a random sample said they would be interested in the new plan. This means the fraction of sampled customers who said they would be interested is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 8 Over 300 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>300</mn></mfrac></math>. Multiplying this fraction by the total customer population yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis StartFraction 8 Over 300 EndFraction right parenthesis left parenthesis 30,000 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>300</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>30,000</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"800\"><mn>800</mn></math>. Therefore, the best estimate of the total number of customers who would be interested in the new service plan is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"800\"><mn>800</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the number of customers surveyed who said they would be interested in the new plan, not the best estimate of the total number of customers who would be interested in the new plan.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","externalid":"f9b50fe8-25d0-4faa-ad54-7ba7d01af7db","correct_answer":["C"]},"createDate":1776362727993,"updateDate":1776362727993}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1776362727993, 1776362727993),
    ($SATQ$55cfaf22$SATQ$, $SATQ$abb8d90e-7d43-41be-9dae-ad5e692240f5$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$ae0211c5-4494-4490-a9d3-1ce39677366d$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$One-variable data: Distributions and measures of center and spread$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: center;">Data set X: <math alttext="5"><mn>5</mn>
</math>, <math alttext="9"><mn>9</mn>
</math>, <math alttext="9"><mn>9</mn>
</math>, <math alttext="13"><mn>13</mn>
</math></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Data set Y: <math alttext="5"><mn>5</mn>
</math>, <math alttext="9"><mn>9</mn>
</math>, <math alttext="9"><mn>9</mn>
</math>, <math alttext="13"><mn>13</mn>
</math>, <math alttext="27"><mn>27</mn>
</math></p>
<p>The lists give the values in data sets X and Y. Which statement correctly compares the mean of data set X and the mean of data set Y?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"98bc1e5f-217b-4671-aa17-66683c49feef","content":"<p>The mean of data set X is greater than the mean of data set Y.</p>"},{"id":"0362b154-b640-4629-83fd-851453b4ccd3","content":"<p>The mean of data set X is less than the mean of data set Y.</p>"},{"id":"e5609ddc-55a0-4a73-b7f9-8c960a790a29","content":"<p>The means of data set X and data set Y are equal.</p>"},{"id":"a81bf904-1905-451c-a9e2-ebbf4c933ce0","content":"<p>There is not enough information to compare the means.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["0362b154-b640-4629-83fd-851453b4ccd3"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. ​​The mean of a data set is the sum of the values in the data set divided by the number of values in the data set. It follows that the mean of data set X is <math alttext="StartFraction 5 plus 9 plus 9 plus 13 Over 4 EndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext="9"><mn>9</mn>
</math>, and the mean of data set Y is&nbsp;<math alttext="StartFraction 5 plus 9 plus 9 plus 13 plus 27 Over 5 EndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext="12.6"><mn>12.6</mn>
</math>. Since <math alttext="9"><mn>9</mn>
</math> is less than <math alttext="12.6"><mn>12.6</mn>
</math>, the mean of data set X is less than the mean of data set Y.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Alternate approach: Data set Y consists of the <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> values in data set X and one additional value, <math alttext="27"><mn>27</mn>
</math>. Since the additional value, <math alttext="27"><mn>27</mn>
</math>, is larger than any value in data set X, the mean of data set X is less than the mean of data set Y.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"55cfaf22","external_id":"abb8d90e-7d43-41be-9dae-ad5e692240f5","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"ae0211c5-4494-4490-a9d3-1ce39677366d","uId":"98b85f4b-3df7-4134-ad99-0b24b83bf7f6","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.C.","skill_desc":"One-variable data: Distributions and measures of center and spread","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\">Data set X: <math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"13\"><mn>13</mn>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\">Data set Y: <math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"13\"><mn>13</mn>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"27\"><mn>27</mn>\n</math></p>\n<p>The lists give the values in data sets X and Y. Which statement correctly compares the mean of data set X and the mean of data set Y?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"98bc1e5f-217b-4671-aa17-66683c49feef","content":"<p>The mean of data set X is greater than the mean of data set Y.</p>"},{"id":"0362b154-b640-4629-83fd-851453b4ccd3","content":"<p>The mean of data set X is less than the mean of data set Y.</p>"},{"id":"e5609ddc-55a0-4a73-b7f9-8c960a790a29","content":"<p>The means of data set X and data set Y are equal.</p>"},{"id":"a81bf904-1905-451c-a9e2-ebbf4c933ce0","content":"<p>There is not enough information to compare the means.</p>"}],"keys":["0362b154-b640-4629-83fd-851453b4ccd3"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. ​​The mean of a data set is the su