    ($SATQ$566759ef$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$05321-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Percentages$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">Thomas installed a new stove in his restaurant. At the time of installation, the stove had a value of $800. Thomas estimates that each year the value of the stove will depreciate by 20% of the previous year&rsquo;s estimated value. What is the estimated value of the stove exactly 2&nbsp;years after Thomas installed it?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">$480</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">$512</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">$556</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">$640</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. If the stove&rsquo;s value depreciates by 20% of the previous year&rsquo;s estimated value, then each year it retains 100% &ndash; 20% = 80%, or 0.80, of the previous year&rsquo;s estimated value. Since the stove&rsquo;s value was $800 when Thomas installed it, the estimated value after two years would be (0.80)(0.80)($800) = $512.<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of the stove if each year it had depreciated by 20% of the original value rather than by 20% of the previous year&rsquo;s estimated value. Choice C is incorrect and may be the result of a computational error. Choice D is incorrect. This is the estimated value of the stove 1 year after Thomas installed it, not 2 years.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
