    ($SATQ$58171b5e$SATQ$, $SATQ$741f638a-272e-4982-91a9-50a01668f587$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$168dd872-e7b4-4bae-a046-b8445e51f634$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.D.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Each year, the value of an investment increases by <math alttext="0.49 percent sign"><mn>0.49</mn>
<mo>%</mo></math> of its value the previous year. Which of the following functions best models how the value of the investment changes over time?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"d2ad14a3-8202-478f-8e54-ef06930d8e2c","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Decreasing exponential</p>"},{"id":"539d55ba-d126-48bc-83e8-7909cc64466b","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Decreasing linear</p>"},{"id":"41055827-b2cd-4fab-8685-09485b045b44","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Increasing exponential</p>"},{"id":"0bd39721-4805-46be-8d4c-8701054b7372","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Increasing linear</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["41055827-b2cd-4fab-8685-09485b045b44"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is correct. Because the value of the investment increases each year, the function that best models how the value of the investment changes over time is an increasing function. It&prime;s given that each year, the value of the investment increases by <math alttext="0.49 percent sign"><mn>0.49</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of its value the previous year. Since the value of the investment changes by a fixed percentage each year, the function that best models how the value of the investment changes over time is an exponential function. Therefore, the function that best models how the value of the investment changes over time is an increasing exponential function.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>
<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"58171b5e","external_id":"741f638a-272e-4982-91a9-50a01668f587","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"168dd872-e7b4-4bae-a046-b8445e51f634","uId":"f055e587-6355-4327-997f-d47cbc5762c1","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.D.","skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Each year, the value of an investment increases by <math alttext=\"0.49 percent sign\"><mn>0.49</mn>\n<mo>%</mo></math> of its value the previous year. Which of the following functions best models how the value of the investment changes over time?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"d2ad14a3-8202-478f-8e54-ef06930d8e2c","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Decreasing exponential</p>"},{"id":"539d55ba-d126-48bc-83e8-7909cc64466b","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Decreasing linear</p>"},{"id":"41055827-b2cd-4fab-8685-09485b045b44","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Increasing exponential</p>"},{"id":"0bd39721-4805-46be-8d4c-8701054b7372","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Increasing linear</p>"}],"keys":["41055827-b2cd-4fab-8685-09485b045b44"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is correct. Because the value of the investment increases each year, the function that best models how the value of the investment changes over time is an increasing function. It&prime;s given that each year, the value of the investment increases by <math alttext=\"0.49 percent sign\"><mn>0.49</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of its value the previous year. Since the value of the investment changes by a fixed percentage each year, the function that best models how the value of the investment changes over time is an exponential function. Therefore, the function that best models how the value of the investment changes over time is an increasing exponential function.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":"manifold","position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959835,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"58171b5e","skill_cd":"Q.D.","score_band_range_cd":5,"skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","createDate":1691007959835,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":null,"external_id":"741f638a-272e-4982-91a9-50a01668f587","primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"f055e587-6355-4327-997f-d47cbc5762c1","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"keys":["41055827-b2cd-4fab-8685-09485b045b44"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is correct. Because the value of the investment increases each year, the function that best models how the value of the investment changes over time is an increasing function. It&prime;s given that each year, the value of the investment increases by <math alttext=\"0.49 percent sign\"><mn>0.49</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of its value the previous year. Since the value of the investment changes by a fixed percentage each year, the function that best models how the value of the investment changes over time is an exponential function. Therefore, the function that best models how the value of the investment changes over time is an increasing exponential function.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>","origin":"manifold","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Each year, the value of an investment increases by <math alttext=\"0.49 percent sign\"><mn>0.49</mn>\n<mo>%</mo></math> of its value the previous year. Which of the following functions best models how the value of the investment changes over time?</p>","externalid":"741f638a-272e-4982-91a9-50a01668f587","templateid":"e8ae768a-2bb3-411d-8f3f-7983fc20f40e","vaultid":"168dd872-e7b4-4bae-a046-b8445e51f634","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"d2ad14a3-8202-478f-8e54-ef06930d8e2c","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Decreasing exponential</p>"},{"id":"539d55ba-d126-48bc-83e8-7909cc64466b","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Decreasing linear</p>"},{"id":"41055827-b2cd-4fab-8685-09485b045b44","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Increasing exponential</p>"},{"id":"0bd39721-4805-46be-8d4c-8701054b7372","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Increasing linear</p>"}],"correct_answer":["C"]},"createDate":1691007959835,"updateDate":1691007959835}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959835, 1691007959835),
    ($SATQ$585de39a$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$070921-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.E.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Probability and conditional probability$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">On May 10, 2015, there were 83 million Internet subscribers in Nigeria. The major Internet providers were MTN, Globacom, Airtel, Etisalat, and Visafone. By September 30, 2015, the number of Internet subscribers in Nigeria had increased to 97 million. If an Internet subscriber in Nigeria on September 30, 2015, is selected at random, the probability that the person selected was an MTN subscriber is 0.43. There were <span class="italic">p</span> million MTN subscribers in Nigeria on September 30, 2015. To the nearest integer, what is the value of <span class="italic">p </span>?</p>
$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["42"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>The correct answer is 42. It&rsquo;s given that in Nigeria on September 30, 2015, the probability of selecting an MTN subscriber from all Internet subscribers is 0.43, that there were <span class="italic">p</span> million, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/585de39a/img_000_6395d088.png" alt="p of 1,000,000"></span>, MTN subscribers, and that there were 97 million, or 97,000,000, Internet subscribers. The probability of selecting an MTN subscriber from all Internet subscribers can be found by dividing the number of MTN subscribers by the total number of Internet subscribers. Therefore, the equation <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/585de39a/img_001_07cc3d0f.png" alt="the fraction with numerator p of 1,000,000, and denominator 97,000,000, equals 0 point 4 3"></span> can be used to solve for <span class="italic">p</span>. Dividing 1,000,000 from the numerator and denominator of the expression on the left-hand side yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/585de39a/img_002_41fe0571.png" alt="the fraction p over 97, equals 0 point 4 3"></span>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by 97 yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/585de39a/img_003_166e8c63.png" alt="p equals, 0 point 4 3 times 97, which equals 41 point 7 1"></span>, which, to the nearest integer, is 42.</p>
$SATQ$, true, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$SPR$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"585de39a","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"070921-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.E.","skill_desc":"Probability and conditional probability","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">On May 10, 2015, there were 83 million Internet subscribers in Nigeria. The major Internet providers were MTN, Globacom, Airtel, Etisalat, and Visafone. By September 30, 2015, the number of Internet subscribers in Nigeria had increased to 97 million. If an Internet subscriber in Nigeria on September 30, 2015, is selected at random, the probability that the person selected was an MTN subscriber is 0.43. There were <span class=\"italic\">p</span> million MTN subscribers in Nigeria on September 30, 2015. To the nearest integer, what is the value of <span class=\"italic\">p </span>?</p>\n","answerOptions":null,"keys":null,"correct_answer":["42"],"rationale":"<p>The correct answer is 42. It&rsquo;s given that in Nigeria on September 30, 2015, the probability of selecting an MTN subscriber from all Internet subscribers is 0.43, that there were <span class=\"italic\">p</span> million, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/585de39a/img_000_6395d088.png\" alt=\"p of 1,000,000\"></span>, MTN subscribers, and that there were 97 million, or 97,000,000, Internet subscribers. The probability of selecting an MTN subscriber from all Internet subscribers can be found by dividing the number of MTN subscribers by the total number of Internet subscribers. Therefore, the equation <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/585de39a/img_001_07cc3d0f.png\" alt=\"the fraction with numerator p of 1,000,000, and denominator 97,000,000, equals 0 point 4 3\"></span> can be used to solve for <span class=\"italic\">p</span>. Dividing 1,000,000 from the numerator and denominator of the expression on the left-hand side yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/585de39a/img_002_41fe0571.png\" alt=\"the fraction p over 97, equals 0 point 4 3\"></span>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by 97 yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/585de39a/img_003_166e8c63.png\" alt=\"p equals, 0 point 4 3 times 97, which equals 41 point 7 1\"></span>, which, to the nearest integer, is 42.</p>\n","answer_style":"SPR","section":"Math","image_count":4,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959633,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"585de39a","skill_cd":"Q.E.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Probability and conditional probability","createDate":1691007959633,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"070921-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"79099f40-e60b-47fe-85e2-4e4c3bfdad51","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"070921-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">On May 10, 2015, there were 83 million Internet subscribers in Nigeria. The major Internet providers were MTN, Globacom, Airtel, Etisalat, and Visafone. By September 30, 2015, the number of Internet subscribers in Nigeria had increased to 97 million. If an Internet subscriber in Nigeria on September 30, 2015, is selected at random, the probability that the person selected was an MTN subscriber is 0.43. There were <span class=\"italic\">p</span> million MTN subscribers in Nigeria on September 30, 2015. To the nearest integer, what is the value of <span class=\"italic\">p </span>?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"SPR","rationale":"<p>The correct answer is 42. It&rsquo;s given that in Nigeria on September 30, 2015, the probability of selecting an MTN subscriber from all Internet subscribers is 0.43, that there were <span class=\"italic\">p</span> million, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"p of 1,000,000\"></span>, MTN subscribers, and that there were 97 million, or 97,000,000, Internet subscribers. The probability of selecting an MTN subscriber from all Internet subscribers can be found by dividing the number of MTN subscribers by the total number of Internet subscribers. Therefore, the equation <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction with numerator p of 1,000,000, and denominator 97,000,000, equals 0 point 4 3\"></span> can be used to solve for <span class=\"italic\">p</span>. Dividing 1,000,000 from the numerator and denominator of the expression on the left-hand side yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction p over 97, equals 0 point 4 3\"></span>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by 97 yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"p equals, 0 point 4 3 times 97, which equals 41 point 7 1\"></span>, which, to the nearest integer, is 42.</p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959633,"updateDate":1691007959633,"correct_answer_extracted_from_rationale":true}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959633, 1691007959633),
    ($SATQ$58a71e06$SATQ$, $SATQ$058dbe26-68a9-4661-8276-5e77b75ac679$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Percentages$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Of <math alttext="300,000"><mn>300,000</mn>
</math> paper clips, <math alttext="234,000"><mn>234,000</mn>
</math> are size large. What percentage of the paper clips are size large?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"ebfb48e8-8b35-4101-97a4-db8621f0c754","content":"<p><math alttext=\"22 percent sign\"><mn>22</mn>\n<mo>%</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"4011921b-ab9e-4e5f-a64e-d6a39bbdf8d1","content":"<p><math alttext=\"33 percent sign\"><mn>33</mn>\n<mo>%</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"9a0aca5f-e0a4-41d5-b1c6-ee150b939a42","content":"<p><math alttext=\"66 percent sign\"><mn>66</mn>\n<mo>%</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"2f83d957-6612-4a33-b122-65232be42120","content":"<p><math alttext=\"78 percent sign\"><mn>78</mn>\n<mo>%</mo></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["2f83d957-6612-4a33-b122-65232be42120"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. The proportion of the paper clips that are size large can be written as <math alttext="StartFraction 234,000 Over 300,000 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>234,000</mn><mn>300,000</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext="0.78"><mn>0.78</mn>
</math>. Therefore, the percentage of the paper clips that are size large is <math alttext="0.78 left parenthesis 100 right parenthesis"><mn>0.78</mn><mfenced><mn>100</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext="78 percent sign"><mn>78</mn><mo>%</mo></math>.</p>
