est weights, so decreasing the lowest weight would increase the range. Choice D is incorrect. Standard deviation is calculated based on the mean weight of the horses. Decreasing one of the weights decreases the mean and therefore would affect the standard deviation.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959616,"updateDate":1691007959616}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959616, 1691007959616),
    ($SATQ$5dc386fb$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$022848-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.E.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Probability and conditional probability$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<div class="stimulus_reference " xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1">
	<div class="passage ">
		<div class="prose style:1 ">
			<p class="passage_para ">The table below shows the distribution of US states according to whether they have a state-level sales tax and a state-level income tax.</p>

			<table class="table_WithBorder">
				<caption>2013 State-Level Taxes</caption>
				<tbody>
					<tr>
						<td class="tcp-153694c7-8fa3-4e23-94a4-6ea6e2e697de">&nbsp;</td>
						<td class="tcp-e5a53952-9288-40e0-ac19-cafecda65b9b">State sales tax</td>
						<td class="tcp-10ebc204-0eda-4bce-ba75-826a9b8a2a82">No state sales tax</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="tcp-90f074ad-6769-4a50-ae37-618ca7ff7b31">State income tax</td>
						<td class="tcp-97ba8e95-d3bf-4293-b928-e12feb1f5419">39</td>
						<td class="tcp-1b3bda3e-5a56-499a-a798-bbd993270702">4</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="tcp-c1409411-06b0-4363-89b8-171abff0b8c0">No state income tax</td>
						<td class="tcp-43b1ecd9-27b9-4264-9eac-617d6bce776a">6</td>
						<td class="tcp-6256a8c4-7f90-4037-ae03-64c4afd368b8">1</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>

			<p class="passage_para ">&nbsp;</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">To the nearest tenth of a percent, what percent of states with a state-level sales tax do not have a state-level income tax?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">6.0%</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">12.0%</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">13.3%</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">14.0%</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is correct. The sum of the number of states with a state-level sales tax is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/5dc386fb/img_000_b0b73e86.png" alt="39 plus 6, equals 45"></span>. Of these states, 6 don&rsquo;t have a state-level income tax. Therefore, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/5dc386fb/img_001_00e21fe2.png" alt="6 over 45, equals 0 point 1 3 3 3 dot dot dot"></span>, or about 13.3%, of states with a state-level sales tax don&rsquo;t have a state-level income tax.<p><br>
	Choice A is incorrect. This is the number of states that have a state-level sales tax and no state-level income tax. Choice B is incorrect. This is the percent of states that have a state-level sales tax and no state-level income tax. Choice D is incorrect. This is the percent of states that have no state-level income tax.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
