<div role="region" aria-label="Long description for graph of a curve" class="sr-only"><ul><li>Moving from left to right:<br>
<ul>
<li>The curve passes from quadrant 2 to quadrant 1.</li>
<li>In quadrant 2, the curve trends up gradually to point (0 comma 1).</li>
<li>In quadrant 1, the curve trends up sharply.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>As x decreases, the curve approaches the line y equals 0.</li>
<li>The curve passes through the following points:<br>
<ul>
<li>approximately (negative 1 comma 0.2)</li>
<li>(0 comma 1)</li>
<li>approximately (1 comma 5.3)</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul></div></figure></span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Which of the following best describes the function <math alttext="f"><mi>f</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"e5eaf552-5659-4593-bdbc-7853f6088848","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Decreasing exponential</p>"},{"id":"58094d94-ec19-4876-9b39-a5c38c9a3f2a","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Increasing exponential</p>"},{"id":"4cc46ea0-caa9-420c-a7ea-a8e308d87dbc","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Decreasing linear</p>"},{"id":"46eae8cb-e32b-43cc-8652-2253e570eed0","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Increasing linear</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["58094d94-ec19-4876-9b39-a5c38c9a3f2a"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. The graph of function <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f"><mi>f</mi></math> shows that as <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> increases, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> also increases, which means that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f"><mi>f</mi></math> is an increasing function. The graph of function <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f"><mi>f</mi></math> is curved upward and increases at an increasing rate, not a constant rate. This behavior is characteristic of exponential functions, not linear functions. Therefore, of the given choices, function <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f"><mi>f</mi></math> is best described as increasing exponential.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect. For a decreasing function, as <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> increases,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> decreases rather than increases.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect. For a decreasing function, as&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> increases,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> decreases rather than increases, and the graph of a linear function isn't curved.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect. The graph of a linear function isn't curved.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"632cf8f9","external_id":"3197f818-b46b-411b-ba07-d4d1c811fa29","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"249a7994-b7e3-4b44-8ae6-a55ba9d163b5","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.D.","skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The graph of the function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> is shown, where <math alttext=\"y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg height=\"275.22pt\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 287.764248 275.22\" width=\"287.764248pt\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Graph of a curve in the x y plane with the origin labeled O. The x axis ranges from negative 6 to 3 in increments of 1, with values marked every 2 grid lines. The y axis ranges from negative 2 to 6 in increments of 1, with values marked every 2 grid lines. Refer to long description.\">\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">\n*{stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:round;}\n  </style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M -0 275.22 \nL 287.764248 275.22 \nL 287.764248 0 \nL -0 0 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 8.404248 260.46 \nL 280.564248 260.46 \nL 280.564248 10.98 \nL 8.404248 10.98 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"></g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_2\"></g>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_2\">\n   