97 41.148707 \nL 203.0406 36.377083 \nL 203.0406 36.377083 \n\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-linecap:square;stroke-width:2.3;\"></path>\n   </g>\n  </g>\n </g>\n <defs>\n  <clipPath id=\"p0d6c2b243f\">\n   <rect height=\"260.82\" width=\"268.898496\" x=\"7.2\" y=\"7.2\"></rect>\n  </clipPath>\n </defs>\n</svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for graph of a curve\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>Moving from left to right:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>The curve passes from quadrant 2 to quadrant 1.</li>\n<li>In quadrant 2, the curve trends up gradually to point (0 comma 1).</li>\n<li>In quadrant 1, the curve trends up sharply.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>As x decreases, the curve approaches the line y equals 0.</li>\n<li>The curve passes through the following points:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>approximately (negative 1 comma 0.2)</li>\n<li>(0 comma 1)</li>\n<li>approximately (1 comma 5.3)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></div></figure></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Which of the following best describes the function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"e5eaf552-5659-4593-bdbc-7853f6088848","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Decreasing exponential</p>"},{"id":"58094d94-ec19-4876-9b39-a5c38c9a3f2a","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Increasing exponential</p>"},{"id":"4cc46ea0-caa9-420c-a7ea-a8e308d87dbc","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Decreasing linear</p>"},{"id":"46eae8cb-e32b-43cc-8652-2253e570eed0","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Increasing linear</p>"}],"keys":["58094d94-ec19-4876-9b39-a5c38c9a3f2a"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. The graph of function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math> shows that as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> increases, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> also increases, which means that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math> is an increasing function. The graph of function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math> is curved upward and increases at an increasing rate, not a constant rate. This behavior is characteristic of exponential functions, not linear functions. Therefore, of the given choices, function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math> is best described as increasing exponential.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect. For a decreasing function, as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> increases,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> decreases rather than increases.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect. For a decreasing function, as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> increases,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> decreases rather than increases, and the graph of a linear function isn't curved.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. The graph of a linear function isn't curved.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1776362727992,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"632cf8f9","skill_cd":"Q.D.","score_band_range_cd":3,"skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","createDate":1776362727992,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"","external_id":"3197f818-b46b-411b-ba07-d4d1c811fa29","primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"249a7994-b7e3-4b44-8ae6-a55ba9d163b5","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The graph of the function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> is shown, where <math alttext=\"y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg height=\"275.22pt\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 287.764248 275.22\" width=\"287.764248pt\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Graph of a curve in the x y plane with the origin labeled O. The x axis ranges from negative 6 to 3 in increments of 1, with values marked every 2 grid lines. The y axis ranges from negative 2 to 6 in increments of 1, with values marked every 2 grid lines. Refer to long description.\">\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">\n*{stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:round;}\n  </style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M -0 275.22 \nL 287.764248 275.22 \nL 287.764248 0 \nL -0 0 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 8.404248 260.46 \nL 280.564248 260.46 \nL 280.564248 10.98 \nL 8.404248 10.98 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"></g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_2\"></g>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_2\">\n   <g id=\"patch_3\">\n    <path d=\"M 7.2 268.02 \nL 276.098496 268.02 \nL 276.098496 7.2 \nL 7.2 7.2 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_3\">\n    <g id=\"xtick_1\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick_2\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick_3\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick_4\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick_5\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick_6\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick_7\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick_8\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick_9\"></g>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_4\">\n    <g id=\"ytick_1\"></g>\n    <g id=\"ytick_2\"></g>\n    <g id=\"ytick_3\"></g>\n    <g id=\"ytick_