.21875 -7.03125 \nQ 22.46875 -3.71875 22.46875 6.0625 \nQ 22.46875 10.84375 22.21875 15.578125 \nQ 21.96875 20.3125 21.328125 25.296875 \nQ 20.703125 30.28125 19.484375 33.34375 \nQ 18.265625 36.421875 16.609375 36.421875 \nQ 15.71875 36.421875 13.953125 34.765625 \nQ 12.203125 33.109375 11.234375 31.84375 \nQ 11.03125 31.84375 10.5 32.765625 \nQ 9.96875 33.6875 9.96875 34.078125 \nQ 10.546875 35.546875 14.59375 39.015625 \nQ 18.65625 42.484375 21.09375 42.484375 \nz\n\" id=\"CrimsonText-Italic-121\"></path>\n     </defs>\n     <g transform=\"translate(174.161652 22.350767)scale(0.15 -0.15)\">\n      <use xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Italic-121\"></use>\n     </g>\n    </g>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"text_23\">\n    <g clip-path=\"url(#p0d6c2b243f)\">\n     <!-- x -->\n     <defs>\n      <path d=\"M 20.3125 42.484375 \nQ 24.421875 42.484375 26.953125 33.984375 \nL 29 27.046875 \nL 34.765625 36.921875 \nQ 37.984375 42.484375 42.96875 42.484375 \nQ 46.296875 42.484375 48.640625 40.53125 \nQ 49.421875 38.96875 49.421875 37.984375 \nQ 49.421875 36.53125 48.390625 35.5 \nQ 47.359375 34.46875 46.296875 34.46875 \nQ 45.015625 34.46875 43.40625 35.984375 \nQ 41.796875 37.5 40.4375 37.5 \nQ 39.265625 37.5 37.796875 34.96875 \nL 30.46875 22.46875 \nL 34.671875 8.6875 \nQ 35.640625 5.375 37.3125 5.375 \nQ 38.765625 5.375 40.421875 6.890625 \nQ 42.09375 8.40625 42.78125 9.671875 \nQ 43.171875 9.671875 43.75 8.890625 \nQ 44.34375 8.109375 44.34375 7.71875 \nQ 44.046875 6.0625 40.71875 2.78125 \nQ 37.40625 -0.484375 34.375 -0.484375 \nQ 30.28125 -0.484375 27.734375 8.015625 \nL 25.484375 15.625 \nL 19.34375 4.984375 \nQ 16.109375 -0.59375 11.140625 -0.59375 \nQ 7.8125 -0.59375 5.46875 1.375 \nQ 4.6875 2.734375 4.6875 3.90625 \nQ 4.6875 5.375 5.703125 6.390625 \nQ 6.734375 7.421875 7.8125 7.421875 \nQ 9.078125 7.421875 10.6875 5.90625 \nQ 12.3125 4.390625 13.671875 4.390625 \nQ 14.84375 4.390625 16.3125 6.9375 \nL 24.03125 20.21875 \nL 20.015625 33.296875 \nQ 19.046875 36.625 17.390625 36.625 \nQ 15.921875 36.625 14.25 35.109375 \nQ 12.59375 33.59375 11.921875 32.328125 \nQ 11.53125 32.328125 10.9375 33.109375 \nQ 10.359375 33.890625 10.359375 34.28125 \nQ 10.640625 35.9375 13.953125 39.203125 \nQ 17.28125 42.484375 20.3125 42.484375 \nz\n\" id=\"CrimsonText-Italic-120\"></path>\n     </defs>\n     <g transform=\"translate(260.389509 200.707163)scale(0.15 -0.15)\">\n      <use xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Italic-120\"></use>\n     </g>\n    </g>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"line2d_1\">\n    <path clip-path=\"url(#p0d6c2b243f)\" d=\"M 37.782876 197.410667 \nL 101.699349 197.297374 \nL 117.257965 197.063474 \nL 126.929536 196.716025 \nL 134.078089 196.251544 \nL 139.54463 195.696342 \nL 144.170164 195.023562 \nL 148.375195 194.185454 \nL 151.73922 193.307708 \nL 155.103245 192.191169 \nL 158.046767 190.967653 \nL 160.569785 189.693093 \nL 163.092804 188.166446 \nL 165.19532 186.665985 \nL 167.297835 184.922011 \nL 169.400351 182.895003 \nL 171.502866 180.539027 \nL 173.605382 177.800693 \nL 175.707898 174.617948 \nL 177.38991 171.703687 \nL 179.071922 168.41683 \nL 180.753935 164.70974 \nL 182.435947 160.528688 \nL 184.11796 155.813078 \nL 185.799972 150.494564 \nL 187.481985 144.496064 \nL 189.163997 137.730641 \nL 190.84601 130.100239 \nL 192.528022 121.494271 \nL 194.210035 111.788006 \nL 195.892047 100.84077 \nL 197.574059 88.493901 \nL 199.256072 74.568452 \nL 200.938084 58.862597 \nL 202.620097 41.148707 \nL 203.0406 36.377083 \nL 203.0406 36.377083 \n\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-linecap:square;stroke-width:2.3;\"></path>\n   </g>\n  </g>\n </g>\n <defs>\n  <clipPath id=\"p0d6c2b243f\">\n   <rect height=\"260.82\" width=\"268.898496\" x=\"7.2\" y=\"7.2\"></rect>\n  </clipPath>\n </defs>\n</svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for graph of a curve\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>Moving from left to right:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>The curve passes from quadrant 2 to quadrant 1.</li>\n<li>In quadrant 2, the curve trends up gradually to point (0 comma 1).</li>\n<li>In quadrant 1, the curve trends up sharply.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>As x decreases, the curve approaches the line y equals 0.</li>\n<li>The curve passes through the following points:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>approximately (negative 1 comma 0.2)</li>\n<li>(0 comma 1)</li>\n<li>approximately (1 comma 5.3)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></div></figure></span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Which of the following best describes the function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math>?</p>","keys":["58094d94-ec19-4876-9b39-a5c38c9a3f2a"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"e5eaf552-5659-4593-bdbc-7853f6088848","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Decreasing exponential</p>"},{"id":"58094d94-ec19-4876-9b39-a5c38c9a3f2a","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Increasing exponential</p>"},{"id":"4cc46ea0-caa9-420c-a7ea-a8e308d87dbc","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Decreasing linear</p>"},{"id":"46eae8cb-e32b-43cc-8652-2253e570eed0","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Increasing linear</p>"}],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. The graph of function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math> shows that as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> increases, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> also increases, which means that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math> is an increasing function. The graph of function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math> is curved upward and increases at an increasing rate, not a constant rate. This behavior is characteristic of exponential functions, not linear functions. Therefore, of the given choices, function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math> is best described as increasing exponential.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect. For a decreasing function, as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> increases,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> decreases rather than increases.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect. For a decreasing function, as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> increases,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> decreases rather than increases, and the graph of a linear function isn't curved.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. The graph of a linear function isn't curved.</p>","externalid":"3197f818-b46b-411b-ba07-d4d1c811fa29","correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1776362727992,"updateDate":1776362727992}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1776362727992, 1776362727992),
    ($SATQ$63573fea$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$019667-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Percentages$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">During the first month of sales, a company sold 1,300,000 units of a certain type of smartphone. During the same month, 15% of the units sold were returned. If sales and the return rate remain the same for each of the next 5 months, about how many units of this smartphone will be returned to the company during this 6-month period?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">195,000</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">975,000</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">1,170,000</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">6,630,000</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is correct. Of the 1,300,000 units sold during the first month, 15% were returned, so <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/63573fea/img_000_e9690f3d.png" alt="1,300,000 times 0 point 1 5, equals 195,000"></span> units were returned during the first month. If the units were sold and returned at the same rate for the next 5 months, then a total of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/63573fea/img_001_a5f78934.png" alt="195,000 times 6, equals 1,170,000"></span> smartphone units were returned during the 6-month period.<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the number of units that were returned in 1 month. Choice B is incorrect. This is the number of units that were returned in 5 months. Choice D is incorrect. This is the number of units sold and not returned during the first 6 months.</p></p>
